    <string name="help_cloud_title">Community</string>
    <string name="help_cloud_text">Find sounds, presets, projects and tracks shared by others, and share your own: sounds from My sounds, your presets, whole projects or finished tracks. Listening and downloading need no account; publishing and rating do.</string>
    <string name="help_1_title">Channels</string>
    <string name="help_1_text">Each channel is one instrument: drums, a synth, an FM synth, a plucked string, a sampler or an audio track. Tap its name to pick another sound, add effects or rename it.</string>
    <string name="help_2_title">Patterns</string>
    <string name="help_2_text">A pattern is a short loop. Tap the squares to place drum hits. For melodies open the Notes tab and draw notes on the piano roll.</string>
    <string name="help_3_title">Playlist</string>
    <string name="help_3_text">Lay patterns out on the timeline to build the whole track. PAT plays one pattern in a loop, SONG plays the playlist.</string>
    <string name="help_4_title">Mixer</string>
    <string name="help_4_text">Set the volume and panning of every channel and add effects: reverb, delay, compressor, equalizer, pitch correction, 3D sound and more.</string>
    <string name="help_key_title">Key and stereo</string>
    <string name="help_key_text">Choose the key of the song in the menu of the Notes tab or with the chip on the Keys tab: its notes are marked, and notes outside of it can be moved in with one tap. Select notes or an audio clip to set where they sit between left and right. The 3D sound effect moves a sound around your head - in headphones.</string>
    <string name="help_auto_title">Automation</string>
    <string name="help_auto_text">Make the sound change over time: on the Notes tab open the menu, turn on Automation, pick a setting and draw its curve. The setting follows the curve while the pattern plays. An audio track has its curve in the playlist: select one of its clips and tap the curve button.</string>
    <string name="help_lib_title">Your sounds and presets</string>
    <string name="help_lib_text">Add your own audio files to “My sounds” in the studio menu and use them in any project: as an instrument or as a clip in the playlist. Every instrument and effect comes with ready-made presets, and your own settings can be saved as a preset too.</string>
    <string name="help_5_title">Recording</string>
    <string name="help_5_text">Press ● to record: either notes played on the keys and pads, or your voice from the microphone. While the microphone records, a red bar shows the time and the level; the finished take appears on a free track of the playlist.</string>
    <string name="help_6_title">Export</string>
    <string name="help_6_text">When the track is ready, open the menu and export it as WAV, MP3 or M4A - or every channel as a separate WAV. The files appear in the Music/MPS folder. “Save project to a file” puts the project with all its sounds into one .mps file that opens on another phone.</string>
